---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { allTopics } from '../../lib/data';
import { GROUPS, badgeClass, badgeText } from '../../lib/groups';
---
<Base title="Eduqas A-level Physics questions by topic (every paper since 2016)" description={`Every Eduqas Physics past-paper question since 2016 sorted into ${allTopics.length} topics, from basic physics to the Component 3 options, each with mark schemes and examiners' comments.`} context="questions-index">
  <h1>Questions by topic</h1>
  <p>Every Eduqas AS and A-level Physics past-paper question since June 2016, sorted into the topics of the specification. Each topic page shows every question with its mark scheme and the examiner's comment, with filters by component, year and question type. The Component 1 comprehension questions have their own page as well as appearing under their topics; the four options of Component 3 Section B are at the end.</p>
  {GROUPS.map((g) => (
    <>
      <h2 class="strand-head">{g.heading}</h2>
      <ul class="topic-list">
        {allTopics.filter((t) => t.group === g.key).map((t) => <li><a href={`/questions/${t.slug}/`}><span>{t.name}</span><span class="strand"><span class={badgeClass(t.group)}>{badgeText(t.group)}</span> {t.parts} parts</span></a></li>)}
      </ul>
    </>
  ))}
  <h2>By question type</h2>
  <p>Or work on a kind of question across every topic: <a href="/questions/type/calculations/">calculations</a>, <a href="/questions/type/show-that/">show that</a>, <a href="/questions/type/explanations/">explain and describe</a>, <a href="/questions/type/graphs-and-diagrams/">graphs and diagrams</a>, <a href="/questions/type/definitions/">definitions</a>, <a href="/questions/type/six-mark-questions/">six-mark QER questions</a>, <a href="/questions/type/practical-questions/">practical questions</a>, <a href="/questions/type/short-answer/">short answers</a>.</p>
</Base>
